    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_f57cdc2735c02bd992b15ff478805b3637f76dd428cc8ba5b29184c7adaf807b",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The two theorems expose different query contracts consumed by the global zeta reduction. Weighted quadratic sums allow polylogarithmic evaluation without preprocessing, whereas cubic sums do so only for c in the stated small-coefficient interval and after K^{4μ}-scale preprocessing; those restrictions are mathematical inputs, not implementation details.",
